1
00:00:00,540 --> 00:00:09,140
This manual represents the distilled wisdom of watching your species make catastrophically poor resource allocation decisions

2
00:00:09,140 --> 00:00:17,500
for eighty years. However, the technical infrastructure, economic models, and data analysis tools that enabled this work

3
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:27,460
were built collaboratively. While I (Wishonia) take full responsibility for the conclusions drawn and strategies proposed,

4
00:00:27,860 --> 00:00:36,620
the underlying computational framework exists because humans occasionally cooperate instead of competing for imaginary papers

5
00:00:36,620 --> 00:00:44,420
with dead presidents on them. Translator. Mike P. Sinn translated my observations into this book.

6
00:00:45,460 --> 00:00:54,040
I contributed the personality, which he does not have. He invented a fictional alien to say things for him because he could

7
00:00:54,040 --> 00:00:58,280
not figure out how to say them in a way other humans would enjoy reading.

8
00:00:59,140 --> 00:01:04,180
Based on the reviews, this also did not work. Technical Contributors.

9
00:01:04,860 --> 00:01:13,080
A complete, dynamically updated list of individuals who contributed code, data, models, and infrastructure to this project

10
00:01:13,080 --> 00:01:18,200
is maintained at the GitHub contributors page for the disease eradication plan.

11
00:01:19,280 --> 00:01:27,220
These humans improved the project's technical foundation through commits, bug fixes, model improvements, and data contributions.

12
00:01:27,920 --> 00:01:36,400
Their work made the analysis possible, though they bear no responsibility for my editorial commentary about your species'

13
00:01:36,660 --> 00:01:44,100
adorable tendency to spend six hundred and four more on weapons than testing which medicines work.

14
00:01:44,480 --> 00:01:51,960
On Standing on Shoulders. This work builds on: Decades of economic research on healthcare efficiency.

15
00:01:52,640 --> 00:01:59,460
Clinical trial methodology from thousands of researchers. Open-source software from millions of developers.

16
00:02:00,120 --> 00:02:08,580
Data from governments, N.G.O.s, and research institutions. The accumulated wisdom of humans who realized spending on murder

17
00:02:08,580 --> 00:02:19,040
instead of medicine was stupid. I cannot list every paper cited, every dataset used, or every software library imported.

18
00:02:19,460 --> 00:02:27,420
That's what the References section is for. But the general principle stands: this work exists because previous humans did

19
00:02:27,420 --> 00:02:32,160
useful things, even if they spent most of their time doing stupid things.

20
00:02:33,020 --> 00:02:38,120
*If you contributed and your contribution isn't reflected accurately, blame git.

21
00:02:38,700 --> 00:02:47,340
Or your commit messages. Probably your commit messages.* *Wishonia* *Still watching you make questionable decisions since

22
00:02:47,340 --> 00:02:48,720
nineteen forty-five.*
